# Fixtures in tests/fb12/ that this compiler gets wrong today, one per line:
# <fixture> R13-0[b]#NN P0|P1|P2 <one-line symptom>
#
# Same contract as tests/difftest.knownfail, tests/difftest.com.knownfail and
# tests/c99.knownfail: a listed fixture may fail, and a listed fixture that
# starts PASSING is a FAILURE -- closing a defect means deleting its line.
#
# These are the items whose *build shape* is the defect, so difftest's one
# file / one run cannot express them.  Driver: tests/fb12multi.sh.
# Opened 2026-09-30; every fixture reproduces on df8cc9b4.
22-multiple-I R13-0b#22 P1 more than one -I directory is rejected (reject: no such file for #include)
24-nested-quoted-include R13-0b#24 P1 a quoted include resolved relative to the includer is rejected
27-signature-pool R13-0b#27 P1 thirty units exhaust the function signature pool at ctype.h:20
28-anon-struct-static-multiunit R13-0b#28 P1 a file-scope static anonymous struct breaks in a second unit
30-label-defined-twice-miniz R13-0b#30 P1 miniz's four units are rejected (label naming)
23-miniz-deflate-roundtrip R13-0b#23 P0 miniz compress/uncompress round trip: sizeof of a 2-D member row is 8, so dynamic-Huffman deflate blocks are corrupt
36-if-has-feature-toplevel R13-0c#36 P2 E2: #if with a function-like unknown identifier is not covered
35-has-feature R13-0c#36 P2 E2: #if with a function-like unknown identifier is not covered (same E2 gap as 36; the Python side is fixed, the product is not)
34-arm64-fallback R13-0c#34 P0 the arm64 encoder rejects miniz with a fallback message (no position, no construct name); reduced to four units
